        <div id="chemistry" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            6. Is LiFePO4 Better Than NMC for a Power Station?
          </h2>

          <p>
            For home backup, almost always. Most current stations use <strong>lithium iron phosphate</strong> (LiFePO4 or LFP) cells, while older and some premium units use <strong>lithium nickel manganese cobalt</strong> (NMC). The two differ in three places: lifespan, weight and how they behave under heat.
          </p>

